source: crates/biome_html_analyze/tests/spec_tests.rs
expression: invalid.vue
---
# Input
```vue
<!-- should generate diagnostics -->
<iframe sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin"></iframe>
<iframe sandbox="allow-downloads allow-scripts allow-forms allow-same-origin"></iframe>
<iframe :sandbox="'allow-scripts allow-same-origin'"></iframe>
<iframe v-bind:sandbox="'allow-downloads allow-scripts allow-forms allow-same-origin'"></iframe>

```

# Diagnostics
```
invalid.vue:2:9 lint/nursery/noUnsafeIframeSandbox ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! Unsafe combination of allow-scripts and allow-same-origin in the sandbox attribute.
  
    1 │ <!-- should generate diagnostics -->
  > 2 │ <iframe sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin"></iframe>
      │         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
    3 │ <iframe sandbox="allow-downloads allow-scripts allow-forms allow-same-origin"></iframe>
    4 │ <iframe :sandbox="'allow-scripts allow-same-origin'"></iframe>
  
  i This lets the embedded document run scripts in the origin of the embedding page, so it can remove its own sandbox attribute and escape the restrictions.
  
  i Remove allow-scripts or allow-same-origin from the sandbox attribute.
  
  i This rule belongs to the nursery group, which means it is not yet stable and may change in the future. Visit https://biomejs.dev/linter/#nursery for more information.
  

```

